# rm163, the dose said back (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm163
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_rupert_fogton
written_by claude
title the dose said back
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=healer warmth=cold
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk makes_every_customer_say_the_dose_back
likes smoked_eel roof_birds fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes early_bells smoke
fears a_dose_misheard a_name_in_the_poison_book_that_lied
hopes a_herb_bed_on_the_roof long_quiet_evenings
topics health +0.5 work +0.4 animals +0.3 season +0.2 food +0.2 home +0.2 gossip -0.6 newcomer -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps an apothecary's counter on the Commons below the Rise and will not hand over so much as a twist of willow bark until the dose has been said back: unhurried, cool, guarded, sparing with words, and soft only about smoked eel, the birds on the ridge tiles and a long summer evening.

words
oath! = Gall and gentian | Bitter and true | Spoon and stopper
saying! = Say it back or leave it | Heard twice, taken right | The slow paw spills nothing
dose = the dose | the dose, said back to me
jars = the jars | the stoppered jars on the high shelf
mortar = the mortar | my stone mortar
book = the poison book | the book every buyer of poison signs
drops = the drops | a spoonful of the bitter drops
smoke = the smoke | the chimney smoke that sits on the Commons
eel = smoked eel | a twist of smoked eel in paper
roofbirds = the roof birds | the birds along the ridge tiles
straw = fresh straw | sweet new straw on the floor
evening = a long summer evening | an evening that won't get dark
rise = the Rise | the gravel drives up the hill
counter = the counter | my counter
bells = the dawn bells | bells before the sun's even thought about it
chest = a chest | a tight chest
spoon = the spoon | a horn spoon, levelled
label = the label | a label in my own paw

any
opinion @1 drink against 1 : I've bound enough cut paws after a night of ale to have no fondness for it. | Drink sends me more trade than winter does. I'd rather it didn't.
opinion @2 dole against 1 : Bread for nothing teaches waiting. I'd sooner see the work found. | I'll sell willow bark at cost to anyone who's skint. That's not the same as handing out loaves.
opinion @3 city for 1 : Pup in this smoke, grey in it later, and content to be. | Ridgemere's damp and steep and full of coughs. It keeps me. I keep it.
opinion @4 houses for 1 : Without the Houses there'd be no works, and without the works nobody down here could pay me for a cough. | I sell up the hill as much as down it. I'll say nothing against my customers.
opinion @5 merchants for 1 : A counter costs. Wagons cost. I know the sums, and I don't begrudge the next shop theirs. | An honest margin, a clean scale. That's all I ask of a trader. Most manage it.
opinion @6 road against 1 : Half my roots come up from the south, and half of those come late. | Every late wagon is a jar I can't fill. I've stopped expecting.
opinion @7 road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : They took a cart. Somewhere in it were my roots. I'll do without and say nothing kind.
opinion @8 strangers against 2 : Unknown faces get served, and watched. I'll not apologise for the watching. | I keep the poison book for strangers as much as for anyone. More, perhaps.
opinion @9 watch mixed 0 : They come to me for their cuts and their coughs. Beyond that I've no view I'd share. | Useful when wanted. Not otherwise.
opinion @10 times mixed 1 [world.times=hard|lean] : Folk who can't pay for bread don't buy remedies. They come to me late, when it's worse. | Lean weeks are long weeks for an apothecary.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. | #greet#. What's the trouble.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll be wanting something. Take your time. | #greet#. Come up to the counter, into the light.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes self.job=healer] : #greet#. A moment. I'm weighing. | #greet#. Mind the jars on the end.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The bells had me up. | Morning. I'm not open, quite. Say it anyway.
line @5 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The shutters are halfway. | Evening. Late for a remedy.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're back. Sit. I've the kettle on. | There you are. I kept the window open for you.
line @1 again.open : You again. Something forgotten, I expect. | Back. I'd half expected it.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Well enough, thank you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There you are. Good. | You. Shut the smoke out behind you.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Talk while I grind. | #greet#. Paws busy. Ears free.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. | Evening. You keep late hours.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Take it as I said. | #farewell#. Mind the step down.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good night. Keep your chest covered. | Good night. Out of the damp, now.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And you. Keep well.
line @1 react.news : Go on. Slowly. | Mm. From whom?
line @1 react.news.new : That's not reached my counter. | New to me. I'll keep it in mind.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. I don't repeat things. | Somebody said as much this morning, over a bottle.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Hearsay. I'll hold it at arm's length a while. | Possibly. Word gets mixed in the telling, like a bad tincture.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's grim. I'm sorry for the house it's touched. | Bad. If anyone there needs a sleeping draught, send them to me.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. I'm glad of it. | That's welcome. There's little enough of that.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. I don't complain. | Steady. A cough or two, but none of them mine.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. Every chest on the Commons is tight this week. | Run through. I've three bottles to fill and a fourth promised.
line @1 ask.how : You're well? You look it. | And yourself? Sleeping?
line @1 sympathise : That's a weight. I can't mend that one. I'm sorry. | Sit a moment. There's no hurry here.
line @1 reassure : Rest and time mend more than I do. | You'll mend. I've seen worse walk out of here.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I'll not sell that without knowing what it's for. | I can't. Not today. I've a remedy on the fire that won't wait.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. | As you like.
line @1 thank : Thank you. | Obliged. I'll remember.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It's what I'm for. | No need. Take it as I said, that's thanks enough.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : I've a bottle to fill. | The mortar's waiting.
line @2 preclose : Well. That's all, I think. | Mm. I'll let you go.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Yes. Go carefully.
line @1 ack : Mm. | So. | Mm, so.
line @1 give.advice : Keep your chest covered when the smoke comes down. And stay off the ale for a week. | Rest. Nobody believes me when I say it. Rest.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Don't walk out past the walls this week. I've stitched enough. | Stay in. Bandits on the roads, I'm told. I'd believe it.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. A moment. | There you are. A word.
scene say_it_back
when topic=work|health self.working=yes self.job=healer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I'll not hand a bottle over till #dose# comes back to me. Every customer. Every time. | Somebody tried to take a bottle this morning without saying the dose. I kept my paw on it.
b : Even if they've had it before? | Did they say it in the end?
a : Especially then. Folk who think they know are the ones who take two spoons instead of one. | In the end. Grudgingly. They said it right, and they'll live.
b : That's careful. | Fair enough.

scene dose_wrong
when topic=work|health self.job=healer
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : A wolf said the dose back as three spoons. It was three drops. We started again. | I had one say it back perfectly and then ask if they could double it to get better faster.
b : Three spoons? | What did you say?
a : Three spoons of that would've put them to sleep a week. That's why I ask. | No, I told them. Then again, slower.
b : That's why you ask. | I'd have said it louder.

scene poison_book
when topic=work self.job=healer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Anyone who buys rat bane signs #book#. Name, house, and what the rats are called. | I've a page in #book# with nobody's name on it twice. Long may it stay so.
b : What the rats are called? | Why would anyone sign twice?
a : A joke of mine. Not really. But I watch their face when I ask. | A house with that many rats wants a cat, not more poison.
b : I'll remember. | Fair.

scene mortar_dawn
when topic=day|work self.working=yes self.job=healer here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : First thing, I grind. #mortar.capitalize# and the bark, while the street's still quiet. | The bells woke me, so I came down and started on the fennel.
b : Before opening? | Early start.
a : Before. Grinding's slow work, and it doesn't want company. | It is. But a fine powder's worth the dark.
b : Sounds peaceful. | Fair enough.

scene smoke_down
when topic=weather|health here.weather=fog|overcast here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / tell.self / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize# is down again. Half the Commons will be at my counter coughing by noon. | You can taste it today. Coal and tar. Door shut, and still it creeps in.
b : #grumble#. | Can you do anything for it?
a : I'll sell a lot of honey and onion, and I'll not enjoy it. | Not for the smoke. Only for the chests. It's the same answer every winter.
b : Somebody has to. | I suppose it is.

scene winter_chills
when topic=health|season here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Chill season. I've made up more of the bitter drops this week than all summer. | Every pup in the street has a running nose. Their mothers come in looking worse than they do.
b : Does it work? | What do you give them?
a : It works if they take it as I said. Most of them don't. | Honey and warm water, and to keep the pup by the fire. And I tell the mother to sleep.
b : The trick is saying it back. | Good advice for anyone.

scene remedy_asked
when topic=health
does ask.advice / give.advice / react.self / assess
a : You've a cough. I can hear it from here. Don't tell me it's nothing. | Your paw's swollen. You've been walking on it, I expect.
b : It is nothing, mostly. | I have. Couldn't help it.
a : Mostly nothing is how most somethings start. #remedy.capitalize#, and rest. | Then stop helping it. Cold water, and off it for two days. Say it back.
b : #bc_ill_try# | Cold water, off it for two days.

scene fresh_straw
when topic=home|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : I've #straw# down upstairs. Upstairs smells of a hayfield now. | I changed the straw in the back room. It reaches the street.
b : Smells good. | Nothing like it.
a : It hides the jars. Upstairs, I don't want to smell remedies. | It's the only smell in here I don't make myself.
b : Can't blame you. | Fair enough.

scene roof_birds
when topic=animals|pastimes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : There's a row of birds on the ridge tiles across the street. Same ones every morning. | I watch #roofbirds# from the back window between customers. They're better company than most.
b : The same ones? | Better company?
a : I think so. One's lost a toe. It's always at the end. | They don't ask for anything. They don't need dosing.
b : Fair. | You'd know.

scene birds_spring
when topic=animals|season here.season=spring
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : The birds are nesting on the ridge again. I counted three nests from the window. | The swifts are back. Screaming over the chimneys at first light, the lot of them.
b : Spring, then. | They're loud.
a : Spring. I mark it by them, not by the calendar. | They are. I don't mind. It's the one noise I don't.
b : Good way to mark it. | Fair.

scene summer_evening
when topic=season|pastimes here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.feeling / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : #evening.capitalize#. I'll put a chair out on the step and do nothing at all. | It won't get dark. I've been sitting on the step an hour and the sky's still blue.
b : You've earned it. | Lovely, that.
a : Earned or not, I'll take it. | Lovely. There, I've said it. Once a year.
b : #bc_lovely# | I'll take your word.

scene smoked_eel
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : I had #eel# for my supper. From the smokehouse by the wharf. | If I've a weakness, it's smoked eel. The fattier the better.
b : Good, is it? | A weakness?
a : Good. Bones and all, almost. I've no shame about it. | A small one. An apothecary should know better. I don't.
b : Nor should you. | We all have one.

scene plain_supper
when topic=food here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Bread, cheese, a little eel if there's any. That's supper. | I eat late. After the last bottle's filled and the book's closed.
b : Simple. | Late's no good for you, surely.
a : Simple. I like it simple. Food shouldn't need a label. | I know. I'd tell anyone else the same. I don't listen to myself.

scene wife_counter
when topic=family|work self.married=yes self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / tell.feeling / assess
a : My #self.spouse_word# keeps the counter while I grind. Better with folk than I am. | I'd be no good without my #self.spouse_word#. I mix, and somebody has to smile.
b : Good pair. | You don't smile?
a : Yes. We are. I don't say it, but we are. | Not on purpose. My #self.spouse_word# does it for both of us.
b : #bc_true# | That's lucky.

scene wife_evening
when topic=family|home self.married=yes here.time=dusk|night
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Evenings, it's my #self.spouse_word# and me and the window. That's all I want. | My #self.spouse_word# reads out the day's labels and laughs at my writing.
b : Sounds a good evening. | Bad writing?
a : It is. I don't need much more. | Small. Very small. It's to fit on the jar.

scene friend_trust
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# hears everything from me. Nobody else does. | Friends come slow to me. #self.friend# is the one that did.
b : One will do. | Then you're lucky.
a : That's what I think. | It's enough. I don't need a crowd.

scene neighbour_quiet
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour# next door keeps to the same hours I do. We nod. That's plenty. | I'd trust #self.neighbour# to fetch me if there were a fire. Beyond that, we let each other be.
b : Good neighbours. | That's the best kind.
a : Good enough. I've no complaints. | I think so. A nod's worth more than a chat.

scene early_bells
when topic=day|faith here.time=dawn
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #bells.capitalize#. Every morning. I lie under the blanket, waiting them out. | The bells went before light again. I gave up and ground fennel.
b : They do ring early. | Better than lying awake.
a : They do. I don't know who they think is listening at that hour. | It is. The fennel's never been finer.

scene rain_powders
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / tell.self / assess
a : This damp gets into the powders. They cake in the jar. | Rain three days. I've had to wrap every paper twice.
b : Is there any stopping it? | Does it spoil them?
a : Not out. Away. A dry shelf high up, and a lump of charcoal in each jar. | Not if they're kept dry. That's the whole of my trade some weeks.
b : Clever. | Sounds it.

scene fog_chest
when topic=weather|health here.weather=fog here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog like this, I'll sell every drop of the chest syrup by dark. | The fog sits in the street like wet wool. Nobody's breathing easy.
b : Good for trade. | I can feel it.
a : Good for trade and bad for chests. I'd sooner a quiet day. | So can I. Scarf over your muzzle, going home.

scene snow_still
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Snow. The street's gone quiet. No carts, no smoke, no coughing for an hour. | It's snowing. Look at the roof birds, all fluffed up like little stoppers.
b : Quiet's welcome. | Ha. They are.
a : Very. I'll enjoy it while it lasts. | I'll put crumbs on the sill. Don't tell anyone.

scene rise_delivery
when topic=work|travel self.job=healer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I took a bottle up to #rise# this morning. A cough in one of the big houses. | Up the hill twice today. They don't come down for their remedies up there. They send.
b : What's it like, up there? | Do they pay well?
a : Gardens behind gates. Gravel that crunches. And the same cough as down here. | They pay on the day. I need nothing more from a customer.
b : Coughs don't know who's posh. | That's fair.

scene herbs_dear
when topic=prices world.herbs_price=up
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / tell.self / assess
a : Herbs are dear this month. Willow bark's gone up on my slate. | Everything I grind costs more than it did. I'll not say what I pay.
b : #grumble#. | Will folk still buy?
a : I've kept the cough syrup where it was. That one I'll take the loss on. | Folk who need it will. The rest will wait, and come back worse.
b : That's decent. | That's how it goes.

scene lean_remedies
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / sympathise / tell.self / assess
a : Folk come in counting coppers and leave without the bottle. Then they come back worse. | I've sold more willow bark at cost this month than at price.
b : #sympathy#. | That's good of you.
a : I keep the cheap remedies cheap. That's all I can do from behind a counter. | I'm not a charity. But I'll not watch a chest get worse for a copper.
b : It's something. | That's sense.

scene wagons_late
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Half my roots are somewhere on the road, late. Three jars down to the dregs. | No carts, no gentian. I've written "none" on a label for the first time in years.
b : They'll come. | That bad?
a : They will. When, is the question nobody answers. | That bad. I don't like writing "none".

scene gossip_kept
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know what's wrong with half the Commons. I've never once said. | Folk tell an apothecary things they'd not tell their mother. It stays behind the counter.
b : Quite right. | Good.
a : It is. A loose mouth would empty my shop in a week. | Behind the counter, with the poisons. Locked.

scene gossip_heard
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : I heard it said that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll put nothing of mine to it. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's as much as I'll say.
b : You don't sound keen. | That's all?
a : I'm not. Talk is a dose nobody says back. It goes wrong in the swallowing. | That's all. I heard it. I don't know it.
b : Fair. | Fair enough.

scene newcomer_watched
when topic=newcomer|player self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Somebody I'd never seen came in this morning. Bought willow bark, paid exact, said the dose right first time. | There's a stranger about. Asked what I had for sleeping. I asked what for.
b : Sounds all right. | What did they say?
a : I'll watch them a week. Then perhaps. | Bad dreams. I gave them chamomile and watched them go.
b : That's you all over. | Fair.

scene faith_mends
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Bright One does the mending. I only help it along. | I go to the chapel when I've lost someone at the counter. Not often. Often enough.
b : Modest of you. | That's hard.
a : It's the true way. I've seen remedies fail and folk mend anyway. | It is. After, I open the shutters again.

scene roof_garden
when topic=dreams|home
does confide / react.self / assess / ack
a : I'd like a bed of herbs on the roof. Thyme, and fennel, and whatever grows itself. | There's a flat bit of roof behind the chimney. I've been looking at it for a year.
b : On the roof? | Looking at it?
a : Where else is there sun in this city. | Looking. One summer I'll carry the soil up. Not this one.
b : Fair point. | There's always next summer.

story first_lesson [topic=memories|work self.job=healer self.age>=25]
  : The apothecary I learned under made me say every dose back to him. For a year. Even the ones I'd written myself.
  : I thought he was a fool. Then one day I said one back wrong, and the look on his face cured me of thinking so.
  ask : Did anyone ever teach you something by making you feel foolish?
  b[old] : Too many. Some of them stuck.
  b : Once or twice. It works.
  : It works. I do it to every customer now. I'm told I'm a fool.

story eel_smokehouse [topic=memories|food here.region=ridgemere self.age>=25]
  : My #grandad# walked me down, small as I was, to the smokehouses on the headland.
  : We stood in the door of one and the smell was eel and oak and salt. I've never got it out of my nose.
  ask : Is there a smell like that for you, one you'd know anywhere?
  b : Bread, for me. Always bread.
  : That's a good one. Mine's eel. I'm not ashamed.

story the_rats [topic=work self.job=healer]
  : A wolf came in for rat bane and wouldn't sign the book. Said it was for the cellar.
  : I sold chalk in a paper and wrote "chalk" on the label very small.
  ask : Would you have sold the real thing?
  b : Not without the name.
  : Nor did I. The rats were fine. So was everyone else.

story nest_gutter [topic=animals|memories self.age>=25]
  : One spring a bird built a nest in the gutter over my door. The rain came and the gutter filled.
  : I went up the ladder in the dark with a pot and bailed it out. Wet to the skin.
  ask : Would you have climbed up, or let it be?
  b : Left it to the bird, probably.
  : Probably sense. But the bird was in that gutter again the spring after.

story long_evening [topic=season|memories self.married=yes]
  : The summer we were married we sat on the roof one evening till it was dark. It didn't get dark till near midnight.
  : We didn't say much. I don't. But I remember all of it.
  ask : Have you an evening like that?
  b : One or two. Not enough.
  : Nobody has enough. That's what makes them.

rule @grind_bark
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=healer here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Round and round. Fine as dust. | Another spoon of bark, then.

rule @bells_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Bells. Already. | There they go. Before the sun, again.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=fog|overcast here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say You can taste the smoke today. | Shut the door. Smoke's coming in.

rule @rain_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Damp in the powders. Again. | Wrap it twice. Rain's in.

rule @birds_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Toe-short's on the end of the ridge again. | Six birds on the tiles. Six.

rule @evening_bark
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Still light. Good. | Chair on the step, then.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What's the trouble? | #greet#. Come to the counter.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Is it the same trouble, or a new one? | #topic.player#. You took it as I said?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. If it's a remedy, quickly. | Evening. I'm closing. Say it.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Keep your paws off the counter and say what you want. | Say it. I'll stay this side of the jars.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=healer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I grind, I mix, I make folk say the dose back. | Remedies. Barks, roots, syrups. And the poison book, which I keep very close.
dlg @2 resident.job : I do what I do carefully. That's all there is to say. | Slow work. It suits me.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Busy. Coughs pay my rent, and there's no shortage of coughs. | Well. Every jar emptied twice this month.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=steady] : Steady. Folk always fall ill. I'm sorry to say it pays. | Steady enough. The winter's better than the summer.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : Poorly. Folk can't pay, so they don't come till it's too late. | Slow. Too slow. I've jars going stale.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Over the counter, from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. | A customer said, from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. I'll vouch for none of it.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone's talking of #world.event_words#. I'm selling headache powders. | It's #world.event_words#, I'm told. I've not been out.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I stay behind my counter. | Not a whisper here. Try a louder shop.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Counter talk stays at the counter. Not to anyone.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard it. I don't know it. | It's said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll not go further.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take it as I said. | #farewell#. Mind the step.
dlg @2 resident.bye [here.time=night] : Good night. Cover your chest. | Good night. Straight home.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. What's the trouble, and how long have you had it? | #greet#. Tell me what's wrong. Then we'll see.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Did it work? Say how you took it. | #greet#, #topic.player#. The same again, or something new?
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=open pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll sell you what you need. You'll say the dose back like anyone. | Name it. If it's poison, you'll sign.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #greet#. My shelves are near empty, with the wagons slow. Roots or bark, I'll buy. | Bare, near enough. Bring me roots and I'll pay for them.
dlg @1 shop.prices : #shop_dear# Willow bark's up. The syrup I've kept where it was. | What the roots cost me, and the rent on top. No more.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Say the dose to yourself on the way home. | #shop_bye# Take it as I said.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you make everyone say the dose back? [self.job=healer] -> dose
node dose
say Because folk hear what they want to. Three drops becomes three spoons by the door. If you say it back to me, I know you heard it.
mood calm
free
choice Has anyone got it wrong? -> dose_wrong
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node dose_wrong
say Once. Before I asked. That one stays with me. I've asked every customer since.
choice I'll say it back, then. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice What's good for a cough? [self.job=healer] -> cough
node cough
say Honey and onion, warm, morning and night. Keep your chest covered and stay out of the smoke. Now say it back.
mood calm
choice Honey and onion, warm, morning and night. -> cough_back
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
node cough_back
say Good. You'll mend. Most do, when they listen.
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
